= The emergency <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> party congress.

After the disastrous effects of the Wall Street crash, it seems the bourgeoisie parties have gotten the credit for the recovery, not the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span>. So much so that they are now excluded from the national and Prussian government, and their chances of returning are looking bleak. As such, an emergency conference has been held at the request of the so called former "Red Tsar" Otto Braun and the other reformist forces inside the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> to discuss the future direction of the party - specifically, the issue of becoming a Volkspartei. Such change is vehemently protested by the party's Left and Center forces, with recent performances at the ballot box, it looks likely that the conference will result in a victory for the party's right.

- @spd_volkspartei_formed
- @spd_volkspartei_defeated


@spd_volkspartei_formed
title: The <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> reforms itself.
subtitle: Another Volkspartei joins the fray.
unavailable-subtitle: The Left manages to persuade the Center away from the proposal.
choose-if: spd_left < 0
on-arrival: spd_volkspartei = 1; spd_leader = "Braun"; workers_spd -= 5; workers_kpd += 5; unemployed_spd -= 10; unemployed_kpd += 10; new_middle_spd += 10; rural_spd += 10; catholics_spd += 4; pro_republic += 5; spd_relation += 5;

In order to save its electoral chances and potentially reconcile with the German center right, the conference has approved the transformation of the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> into a mass movement, not directed purely at the working class. The Left and some of the Center split, with some joining the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span>, whilst others plan the formation of a new party. The former Center Marxist leadership begrudgingly accepts the change as their influence in the party continues to erode as Otto Braun also becomes the official leader of the party following the same meeting. We can expect the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">socialists</span> to somewhat chip away at our votes, whilst the more radical <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> supporters flock to the <span style="color: #8B0000;">communists</span>.

@spd_volkspartei_defeated
title: The reformist's numbers were smaller than we thought.
subtitle: Instead, it seems the Left is ascendant.
unavailable-subtitle: The Reformists have a majority.
choose-if: spd_left >= 0
on-arrival: spd_return_to_origin = 1; spd_leader = "Seydewitz"; spd_color = "#D47B9B"; workers_spd += 5; workers_kpd -= 5; unemployed_spd += 10; unemployed_kpd -= 10; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 10; rural_spd -= 5; pro_republic -= 5; socialism += 5; spd_relation -= 10;

The recent years have decisively shifted the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> left, not only are the reformists defeated, but the Left successfully pushes a counterproposal of their own. The party will break with its ironclad commitment to the Republic and parliamentarianism, and a revolutionary takeover is, once more, a possibility. In the conference, Max Seydewitz has managed to replace Otto Wels as chairman, in the coming months, we can expect the Reichsbanner to become far more militarized, and ties between the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> and the <span style="color: var(--kpd-color);">**KPD**</span> to strengthen further. <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> support among workers has risen sharply, while decreasing among other demographics
